# THE RUN LOG IS APPEND-ONLY — one section per run, newest at the bottom
# (CLAUDE.md states the rule, and reading the file is denied on purpose because
# it is ~460 KB). Two branches that each append their own run section are not in
# disagreement: BOTH sections belong. `union` is git's built-in driver for
# exactly that — it keeps both sides instead of raising a conflict a person then
# has to resolve by hand inside a file the session may not open.
BUGLOG.md merge=union
